From a8ebea00f1d2094b5ea7d89d01fbccec317c8ed6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:44:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] perf(sim): B2 G2 services: every state in pieces, the
 cost model per piece
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ServicesSystem's states run as pieces of about INFRA_PIECE_MS (the tier
engine) or half INFRA_PIECE_COLD_MS (every other loop: once per pass, so cold
for many passes) estimated warm ms (docs/dev/B2_DESIGN.md §4). The state ids
and transitions are the pre-B2 ones; a pass run with nothing in between
(compute, init, flush) computes exactly what the pre-B2 steps computed.

- prep: the corridor / network / water hashes by ranges (the first piece
  consumes the pass inputs, R5), setup, the back need rasters, traffic's
  pending attachment refresh in a piece of its own, the pass snapshot (R4;
  the per-id arrays sized for every id of it) and its chunk plan, building
  chunks (the 7 need sums as doubles in a Float64Array), the provider need
  runs + their sums, the road count, the publish (need / provNeed swapped
  in: needRaster changes once), the work estimate by facility ranges.
- tiers: units re-weighted to ~uniform cost (U_SEARCH 1.75, report 0.45 per
  entry, init 0.035 per cell, ...); the budget is tested before an item with
  its known units; P_FINAL is items (clamp / stats by rows into a private
  buffer, capacity, the lot max by lots, the publish .set): a tier layer
  changes once, with its lot max.
- stops: the collector over the snapshot and the cells, the disks by stop
  ranges, the compose by rows on a byte copy of transitCov, the publish.
- NIMBY: the nimby.ts run over the pass snapshot.
- access / shops: the seeds over the snapshot, RoadTimeRun / RoadDistRun,
  the chamfer sweeps by rows (each reads only rows it finished), the output
  and the home footprints into private buffers, the publish; shopB's block
  sums and box3 scratch are fields (pre-B2: allocated per call).
- foot / finish: on private buffers, published by .set; stats.needs is
  written with eq / hq in the last piece (saved data in one piece, R9).
- every cursor resets at the pass start (an explicit branch, O8), the pass
  end and init; nothing new is saved. stepName names each piece; cost() is
  pure and mirrors each piece's chunk (SC table x SV_EST, start values).

Tests:
- tests/infra/b2PiecesServices.test.ts: the kernels in random pieces equal
  their originals (RoadTimeRun / RoadDistRun, transit ranges, NimbyRun also
  vs the frozen pre-J4 rebuild, the police need run); three services
  cities (with / without WP1) give identical cities and fields at every
  pass end in one go, at the production size and in tiny / random pieces
  across edits, and equal the frozen original in every original field;
  R8 queries between pieces, R7 one change per state visit, R9 mid-pass
  save, O4 frames vs headless, two cities interleaved, estimates in budget.
- tests/sim/exact/servicesOriginal.ts: services.ts at 41ae570, frozen.
- servicesTrigger 'urgent change after prep', catchments 'bulldozed
  mid-pass': step until prep is done (review 1 R7 b, c).
- servicesTierEngine (WASM): the live-instance sections install the engine
  into the frozen pre-B2 class (its port mirrors that pass structure).
- perf P0-8: services' largest piece estimate <= 1.0 (0.39 measured).

